  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Saturday)\nIssued at 1154 AM MDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nUpper level ridge will remain anchored over the Rockies into the \nPlains supporting hot temperatures through this week. The FA will \nremain on the northern periphery of the ridge with impulses \ntraversing the flow. This will support near daily chances for TS \nas monsoon waves traverse the region. Week sfc trough has advected\nthrough the FA today with winds shifting northerly. This has \nknocked temps down a few degrees from yesterday, but still very \nhot. Weak capping over the BH with sufficient moisture will allow \na few shra/ts to develop there this afternoon. Main focus will be \nthe next impulse expected to support TS this evening in the west. \nTS will develop across WY and push east into the western FA this \nevening. High based nature will support gusty winds as the storms \npush east. As the wave progresses through the FA overnight, sct- \nisold shra/ts will be possible, mainly across the north. Hot \nMonday with temps in the mid to upper 90s once again. The next \nwave will arrive late afternoon/early evening and support TS \nacross the western half, possibly earlier over the BH if \nsubsidence behind tonight's wave has pushed east. Again, gusty \nwinds will be the main threat from TS given continued high based \nnature. Same for each day the rest of the week, daily chances for \nshra/TS as monsoon moisture continues to advect around the \nbackside of the ridge. Most days will see isold-sct activity given\nlack of strong forcing and high based nature of storms. However, \na stronger wave may bring slightly better coverage of storms Wed \ninto Thur if timing works out right. Otherwise, a break in this \npattern and heat is not expected until early next week with a \nstronger northern stream shortwave flattens the ridge and supports\na decent cold front into the Northern Plains.",
